out/build/x64-Debug/VSInheritEnvironments.txt
.gitignore
/debug.cap

# CodeQL artifacts
_codeql_detected_source_root

# vcpkg (issue #773) — per-build-tree installed trees. The manifest (vcpkg.json),
# the custom triplets (cmake/triplets/) and the overlay ports (cmake/overlay-ports/)
# ARE tracked; only the materialised install output is not. The machine-global
# vcpkg clone, downloads/, packages/, buildtrees/ and the binary cache all live
# outside the repo (VCPKG_ROOT / VCPKG_DEFAULT_BINARY_CACHE).
vcpkg_installed/
**/vcpkg_installed/

# Game build output
GameBuilds/
build-*/

OloEditor/cmake_test_discovery_*.json

# Per-user Claude Code state (project-local instructions, skills, agents)
# Ignore the entire .claude/ tree except the shared, version-controlled things:
#   settings.json            — project hooks/permissions config
#   skills/                  — project skills that ship helper scripts (e.g. run-oloengine)
#   commands/                — the workflow slash commands (/start-work, /cleanup-worktree,
#                              /resume-worktrees). These are versioned WITH the repo because
#                              they reference repo content (scripts/issue_scores.py,
#                              docs/process/*, CLAUDE.md) that would otherwise drift.
#   .markdownlint-cli2.jsonc — directory-scoped lint overrides for the front-matter files
#                              under commands/ and skills/ (see the repo-root config).
# Each skill's own .gitignore handles its generated artifacts (screenshots/logs).
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/commands/
!.claude/.markdownlint-cli2.jsonc
.claude/skills/**/shots/
skills-lock.json
docs/agents/

# Generated performance stress scenes (potentially 40+ MB of YAML at 200k
# instances). Only the generator is committed; regenerate on demand with
# OloEngine/tests/scripts/generate_perf_scenes.py.
OloEditor/SandboxProject/Assets/Scenes/PerfStress/

# Binary scene sidecar caches (issue #525). Derived from a scene's `.olo`/`.yaml`
# on load to skip yaml-cpp on subsequent loads; regenerated automatically and
# invalidated when the source changes. Never source-of-truth — do not commit.
*.scenebin

# Generated per-file test catalogues. Rendered from test_catalogue.json + in-file
# // OLO_TEST_LAYER markers by OloEngine/tests/scripts/generate_test_catalogue.py.
# Deliberately NOT committed: the tables change on essentially every test, and a
# tracked generated file made every parallel PR false-conflict on docs/testing.md
# (GitHub ignores the merge=union driver). Regenerate locally on demand.
docs/test-catalogue.*.md

# External assets fetched on demand by scripts/Fetch-Assets.ps1 (see scripts/assets/asset-manifest.json).
# Too large for git history, or licensed to be fetched rather than redistributed.
OloEditor/SandboxProject/Assets/Models/Stanford/

# OloHeaderTool writes each generated artefact to a sibling temp file and renames
# it into place, so two build trees can never expose a half-written .inl. A temp
# only survives a hard kill mid-write; ignore it so it can't be committed by
# accident (tools/OloHeaderTool/main.cpp, issue #758).
*.oht-tmp

# Steamworks (#644). NOTHING from the SDK may ever be committed: this repo is PUBLIC and the
# licence forbids redistribution, so the SDK lives outside the tree entirely, found via
# STEAMWORKS_SDK_ROOT (see docs/ops/build.md). These two are what leak into the tree anyway:
#
# steam_appid.txt — the dev-only App ID (480 = Spacewar) that SteamAPI_Init reads from the
# process working directory, which CLAUDE.md pins to OloEditor/. Valve's guidance is to REMOVE
# it for a release build; the shipped game gets its App ID from the Steam client, and leaving
# it in is how a build accidentally reports itself as Spacewar.
steam_appid.txt
#
# steam_api64.dll — staged next to the executables by the build. It IS the one redistributable
# piece (that is what redistributable_bin/ means), but it is copied from STEAMWORKS_SDK_ROOT at
# build time rather than committed, which sidesteps having to reason about what "redistribution"
# means in a public repo and costs nothing.
steam_api64.dll

# Per-user renderer backend selection written by the Renderer Settings panel (ADR 0011 s2)
OloEditor/config/renderer.yaml

# repowise local index (see issue #815) — ~390MB per checkout, never committed
.repowise/

# C++ coverage artefacts (OpenCppCoverage / Cobertura)
coverage/
